#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:101
msgid "Troubleshooting SMTP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:104
msgid "TLS/STARTTLS requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:106
msgid ""
"If you fill in **SMTP Username** and **SMTP Password** then you must set "
"**Connection Security** to **TLS** or to **STARTTLS**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:109
msgid "Troubleshooting using logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:111
msgid ""
"If you have issues with your SMTP install, from your Mattermost team site"
" go to **System Console > Logs** to look for error messages related to "
"your setup. You can do a search for the error code to narrow down the "
"issue. Sometimes ISPs require nuanced setups for SMTP and error codes can"
" hint at how to make the proper adjustments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:113
msgid ""
"For example, if **System Console > Logs** displays the following error, "
"search for ``554 5.7.1 error`` and ``Client host rejected: Access "
"denied``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:120
msgid "Checking your Notifications settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:122
msgid ""
"If an SMTP connection test in the System Console for a self-hosted "
"Mattermost deployment fails with the message ``Connection unsuccessful: "
"Failed to set the to address: 550 5.7.27 <test@example.com>``, go to "
"**System Console > Site Configuration > Notifications** to verify that "
"notification settings are configured correctly, including **Notification "
"Display Name**, **Notification From Address**, **Support Email Address**,"
" and **Notification Reply-To Address**. Cloud administrators can't manage"
" **Notification From Address** or **Notification Reply-To Address**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:125
msgid "Checking your SMTP server is reachable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:127
msgid ""
"Attempt to Telnet to the email service to make sure the server is "
"reachable. For additional information, visit https://learn.microsoft.com"
"/en-us/exchange/mail-flow/test-smtp-with-telnet?view=exchserver-2019. If "
"you're using an earlier version than Exchange Server 2019, select your "
"version from the left-hand navigation menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:128
msgid ""
"You must run the following commands from the same machine or virtual "
"instance where ``mattermost/bin/mattermost`` is located."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:129
msgid ""
"Telnet to the email server with ``telnet mail.example.com 25``. If the "
"command works you should see something like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:137
msgid ""
"Then type something like ``HELO <your mail server domain>``. If the "
"command works you should see something like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/smtp-email.rst:148
msgid ""
"Telnet isn't included in official Mattermost Docker images, so you either"
" need to use ``ping`` on those, or install Telnet yourself either "
"directly or by modifying the Dockerfile."
msgstr ""

